#basePath Day0

::OpeningPrelude
@trigger    BeginPrelude
@boostScore 100
@cutscene

$wait 3

{@Astrid}	Come on, Elijah, where are you? It's already starting! $[Prelude/Astrid/01]

$call Wait(1)
(*phone buzzing sfx*)
 
{@Elijah}	Astrid, I’m sorry I’m late!
 
{@Astrid}	I was afraid you were going to miss it.

{@Elijah}	Just think... next year on your birthday we'll be in the same place.
{@Elijah}	It's going to be so cool studying astronomy together.

$call Wait(2)
{@Elijah} Did you read my birthday card? I drew you as Perseus. $[Prelude/Elijah/06]

{@Astrid}	It's really great Elijah... though I don't think I'm as tough as Perseus. $[Prelude/Astrid/07]
{@Elijah}	Girl, you're the stuff of Greek myths, ha ha. $[Prelude/Elijah/09]
{@Astrid}	Dudeeeee.

{@Astrid}	Okay, let's focus, the Perseids won't wait for us. Where should I be looking? 
{@Elijah}	Can you find the Perseus constellation? $[Prelude/Elijah/11]
{@Elijah}	Just look for the place where the meteors seem to be coming from.
{@Elijah}	If you move your phone across the sky, it’ll tell you if you’re getting warmer or colder.
 
{@Astrid}	Found it! $[Prelude/Astrid/12]

{@Astrid}	Just imagine... In ancient times they had to map all these stars from scratch. And they used them for navigation, to tell their fates...
{@Astrid}	Must've been a lot of pressure.
{@Elijah}	I don't know. Sounds sort of fun to me.
 
$call Wait(2) 

{@Astrid}	Whoa. Elijah, are you seeing this? $[Prelude/Astrid/20]

{@Elijah}	Astrid—you’re breaking up— $[Prelude/Elijah/20]
 
{@Astrid}	Is that the Northern Lights? $[Prelude/Astrid/21]
{@Astrid}	Whoa. It's so bright!
 
{@Elijah}	(*bzzzzzzz krrrrrrr*) —Something’s not right— $[Prelude/Elijah/21]
{@Elijah}	(*static noises*) —Readings off the charts— (*brrrrrr kzzzzzz*)
 
{@Astrid}	Elijah, can you hear me? $[Prelude/Astrid/22]
$call Wait(2) 
{@Astrid}	Hello? Elijah? $[Prelude/Astrid/23]

$call LoadNextDay()
